      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "content": [
        {
         "type": "text",
         "text": "Hrs Invoiced",
         "marks": [
          {
           "type": "strong"
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "The figures are not missing from the product",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " \u2014 the report has them and can show them. It is only the downloaded file that leaves them out. So this reads as an unfinished download rather than missing data."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Why it matters:",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " these are the counting columns. Somebody working out how many jobs or how many customers a representative handled has to go back to the screen and copy the numbers by hand, which is exactly what the download exists to avoid. The product owner's words when he was shown this were: "
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "\"on-screen should match download\"",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "One more thing in the same file:",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " the spreadsheet also "
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "ends with a Totals row",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": ", which the written description says the Summary version should not have."
    }
   ]
  },
